cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or results obtained with it, please cite it as
  below. Citation is also required by the attribution terms in
  ADDITIONAL-TERMS.md for redistributed or modified versions.
type: software
title: "KAPSAM: open-source software for the evaluation of measurement uncertainty (GUM, Monte Carlo and top-down)"
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/unilker/uncertainty"
authors:
  - family-names: "Ün"
    given-names: "İlker"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5089-4602"
    affiliation: "TÜBİTAK Ulusal Metroloji Enstitüsü (UME), Gebze, Kocaeli, Türkiye"
keywords:
  - measurement uncertainty
  - GUM
  - Monte Carlo method
  - JCGM 101
  - metrology
  - analytical chemistry
  - uncertainty budget
  - software validation
  - ISO/IEC 17025
abstract: >-
  Open-source software for the evaluation of measurement uncertainty: the
  GUM including its 2026 amendment, the Monte Carlo methods of JCGM 101 and
  102, conformity assessment, top-down evaluation, proficiency testing,
  calibration with uncertainty in both variables, precision experiments,
  control charts, uncertainty from sampling, weighing instruments and
  consensus values, with reports in English and Turkish. Validated on 286
  projects built from the worked examples of 38 guidance documents.
